{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 45, "model_name": "nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b", "content": "**A Whirlwind Week in Japan**\n\nLanding in Tokyo felt like stepping into a living postcard. The neon glow of Shibuya Crossing greeted us at night, a sea of people moving in perfect sync despite the chaos. By morning, we traded the bustle for serenity at Meiji Shrine, where towering cedars whispered ancient prayers and the air smelled of incense and rain.\n\nA bullet train whisked us to Kyoto, where time seemed to slow. We wandered through the moss‑covered stones of Ryoan‑ji’s rock garden, each raked line a meditation in simplicity. The golden pavilion of Kinkaku‑ji shimmered against a backdrop of maple leaves turning fiery red, and we sipped matcha in a tiny tea house, feeling the ceremony’s quiet reverence settle into our bones.\n\nNo trip to Japan is complete without food. From steaming bowls of ramen in a hidden alley stall to delicate slices of toro at Tsukiji’s outer market, every bite told a story of precision and passion. We even tried our hand at making sushi in a local workshop, laughing as our clumsy rolls fell apart—only to be rescued by the patient chef’s gentle guidance.\n\nThe final night found us in Osaka, where the Dotonbori canal glittered with neon signs and the aroma of takoyaki floated through the air. We climbed the Umeda Sky Building, watching the city lights stretch out like a galaxy below.\n\nJapan offered a perfect blend of ultra‑modern energy and timeless tradition. Each city revealed a new facet, leaving us with a suitcase full of memories and a heart already planning the next visit.", "logprobs": [{"token": "We", "logprob": -0.19476382434368134}, {"token": " need", "logprob": -0.002491943072527647}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.052601855248212814}, {"token": " produce", "logprob": -1.1176888942718506}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.03277479484677315}, {"token": " short", "logprob": -0.011081226170063019}, {"token"